TNT installation
================

Requirements: a C compiler, CMake 3.20 or newer, Make or Ninja, ncurses
development headers, and system gettext tools (unless TNT_NLS=OFF).
The full native regression suite also requires Python 3.
The interactive setup scripts additionally require dialog.

Configure, compile and test:

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
    cmake --build build --parallel 2
    ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure

Install when ready (with suitable permissions):

    cmake --install build

Use -G Ninja at configuration time for the optional Ninja backend.
Autoconf and Automake are no longer used; do not run ./configure or make in
the source directory. Build artifacts and generated files stay in build/.

Private installation, with all runtime state under your home directory:

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release \
      -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX="$HOME/.local" \
      -DTNT_LOCALSTATEDIR="$HOME/.local/var"

The runtime-state default remains /var, even with a custom installation prefix.
Configuration examples are installed with .ex suffixes and do not replace an
active tnt.ini. No service is installed or started. Existing history is not
removed. Set installation paths when configuring, not via --install --prefix:
paths are embedded in generated examples, setup scripts and binaries.

To stage installation without touching the live system:

    DESTDIR="$PWD/stage" cmake --install build

Feature options, cross-compilation, strict builds and platform notes are
documented in BUILD.md. Existing C flags can be passed via CMAKE_C_FLAGS,
and compilers/toolchains via CMAKE_C_COMPILER or CMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE.

To clean compiled targets:

    cmake --build build --target clean

To uninstall files recorded by this build's installation manifest:

    cmake --build build --target uninstall

Use the same DESTDIR for staged uninstallation. Runtime data and active
configuration files are not part of the install manifest and remain intact.

To start completely fresh, choose a new build directory. Existing Autotools
artifacts from an older checkout are not used by CMake.
